\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {R1}{\ignorespaces Revised case study: girder line of a single-span steel--concrete composite bridge on laminated elastomeric bearings. (a) The seven unknowns are the stiffness reduction factors of the five 2~m deck zones ($z_1,\dots  ,z_5$, which scale the bending stiffness of the zone) and of the two bearings ($z_{b,L}$, $z_{b,R}$, which scale both springs of each bearing), all in $[0.45,1]$. Five vertical accelerometers ($s_1,\dots  ,s_5$, at $x=1,3,5,7,9$~m) identify the first five bending modes (2.5\% noise on the frequencies, 5\% of the peak amplitude on the mode shapes). Every measurement comes from an as-built structure that the nominal decoder does not know: the mass of each 1~m segment is multiplied by $1+\mu _s$, $\mu _s\sim \mathcal  {N}(0,0.05^2)$, and the flexibility of each 0.2~m cell by $1+\varepsilon _c$, $\varepsilon _c\sim \mathcal  {N}(0,0.025^2)$ with zero mean in each zone. Test set B is computed with a 50-element model and localized damage. (b) Cross-section of the deck. (c) Bearing design. The rotational springs are drawn in green.}}{4}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:bridge}{{R1}{4}{Revised case study: girder line of a single-span steel--concrete composite bridge on laminated elastomeric bearings. (a) The seven unknowns are the stiffness reduction factors of the five 2~m deck zones ($z_1,\dots ,z_5$, which scale the bending stiffness of the zone) and of the two bearings ($z_{b,L}$, $z_{b,R}$, which scale both springs of each bearing), all in $[0.45,1]$. Five vertical accelerometers ($s_1,\dots ,s_5$, at $x=1,3,5,7,9$~m) identify the first five bending modes (2.5\% noise on the frequencies, 5\% of the peak amplitude on the mode shapes). Every measurement comes from an as-built structure that the nominal decoder does not know: the mass of each 1~m segment is multiplied by $1+\mu _s$, $\mu _s\sim \mathcal {N}(0,0.05^2)$, and the flexibility of each 0.2~m cell by $1+\varepsilon _c$, $\varepsilon _c\sim \mathcal {N}(0,0.025^2)$ with zero mean in each zone. Test set B is computed with a 50-element model and localized damage. (b) Cross-section of the deck. (c) Bearing design. The rotational springs are drawn in green}{figure.caption.1}{}}
